  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>data_quality - asks a local LLM to check and clean ten customer records, then splits them by its quality
verdict.
Needs Ollama at OLLAMA_URL with MODEL_NAME pulled, and the GenAI plugins with a GENAI-EE license.

1. csvi-customers: CSV file input, ../data_quality_customers.csv, six String fields.
2. js-record: Modified JavaScript value, customer_record = the five values as labeled lines (Name:, Email:,
   Phone:, Address:, Company:).
3. const-instruction: Add constants, run_instruction = the house formats and the JSON shape, with quality
   CLEAN, FIXED or REVIEW.
4. ai-clean: AI Chat x${STEP_COPIES}, Stream message customer_record, run instruction run_instruction,
   Ollama ${MODEL_NAME} at ${OLLAMA_URL}, temperature 0, numCtx 2048, timeout 120, result llm_json.
5. json-clean: JSON input from llm_json: clean_name, clean_email, clean_phone, clean_address,
   clean_company, issues, quality.
6. filter-quality: Filter rows, quality IN LIST CLEAN;FIXED; true to sv-clean, false (REVIEW or no answer) to
   sv-review.
7. sv-clean / txt-clean: the cleaned fields to customers_clean.csv beside this file.
8. sv-review / txt-review: the original fields, quality and issues to customers_review.csv beside this file.
Error hop: json-clean sends an answer it cannot parse to txt-bad-answers: customer_id, llm_json, err_desc
to bad_answers.csv beside this file (0 bytes when every answer parsed).

Shipped data: 10 customers, 1001 to 1010; three emails (1002, 1005, 1008) cannot be valid as given.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>626</width>
      <heigth>386</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
